This is my Linux port of torus, which is robots with a twist--the
playing field 'wraps around', allowing the 'bots to chase you like
there aren't any boundaries.  If you wanna compile it yourself,
make sure your curses lib and libc are properly patched (this is
for gcc 1.40).  Let me know if you have problems; it works fine
for me.  Oh yeah, don't forget to create the high score files using
touch.  The binary in this archive looks for its high score files in 
/usr/games/lib under these names:  torus_hof, torus_tmp, robots2_hof
and robots2_tmp.

